## Report-quality, tunnel, and Brain repair receipt - 2026-06-17

Goal: make the Dreamer HITL report actually good enough to pass the verifier, remove the quick-tunnel footgun from future live deploys, and clear the Brain checker.

Changes:

- `workflow.hitl-report.v1` finding cards now carry `failureClass` and `sourceKind`, so the report has an explicit seam/failure classification instead of relying on prose.
- `joelclaw.memory.hitl-report` now renders refinement-proposal-backed finding cards first and caps fallback search-hit leads at 7. This prevents the live wound where 78 raw search hits became generic findings.
- Search-hit fallback titles no longer say `needs human review`; they render as classified search leads with a concrete next step.
- The post-execution report proof check now fails reports with more than 7 findings, generic review wording, all-10 rating walls, mismatched `findingCount`, or refinement proposals that do not feed any finding card.
- The approved relay provisioning request now rejects Cloudflare Quick Tunnel hostnames (`*.trycloudflare.com`) with blocker `memory-relay-base-url-ephemeral-quick-tunnel`.
- `scripts/workflow-app-deploy-and-seed.mjs` now refuses `MEMORY_RELAY_BASE_URL` values on `*.trycloudflare.com` before Wrangler deploy can run.
- The provisioning plan text now asks for a stable HTTPS hostname: Cloudflare named tunnel DNS route, static ngrok domain, or equivalent.
- Unsupported Brain support files were converted from `.md` to valid `.svx` resources:
  - `.brain/resources/phase1a-drive-ledger-spec.svx`
  - `.brain/resources/phase1b-chaos-harness-spec.svx`

